@startuml bootwire_erase_sequence
!include ../_style.iuml
title <size:21><color:#1B3A5F><b>ERASE</b></color></size>\n<size:13><color:#5B6B7C>one command per erase block, each answered within erase_timeout</color></size>
!include _participants.iuml

autonumber "<b>00"
APP -> HOST : erase_region(0x08008000, 20000)
HOST -> HOST : check the range is inside the application region\nround out to whole blocks: 10 × 2048 bytes
loop for each erase block
  HOST -> TP : ERASE [SEQ, address, 2048]\n(timeout = erase_timeout)
  activate TP
  TP -> TP : payload is 8 bytes?\naddress and length block-aligned?\ninside the application region?
  alt a check fails
    TP --> HOST : [SEQ, 0x90, <color:#C0392B><b>BAD_LENGTH</b></color> or <color:#C0392B><b>BAD_PARAM</b></color>]
    HOST --> APP : BootWireStatusError (nothing erased)
  else checks pass
    TP -> BL : erase the block
    BL --> TP : result
    alt erase failed
      TP --> HOST : [SEQ, 0x90, <color:#C0392B><b>FLASH</b></color>]
      HOST --> APP : BootWireStatusError
    else erased
      TP --> HOST : [SEQ, 0x90, <color:#1E8449><b>OK</b></color>]
      deactivate TP
      HOST -> APP : progress("erase", done, total)
    end
  end
end
note over HOST, BL
  One block per command keeps every response quick (a page or sector erase),
  so one timeout fits all parts. A full-region erase in one command could take
  seconds, longer than the host can tell from a lost frame.
end note
@enduml
